It is Sunday evening.
Anitha comes to my flat.
Tommy is very happy when he sees Anitha.
He runs to her.
"Tommy didn't make any trouble, right?" Anitha asks.
"No, he was a very good boy," I say with a smile.
"He perfectly obeyed all the rules."
"He must not be given sweet snacks, right."
"So I did not give him anything."
"When going outside, he must always be taken on the leash."
"I always took him like that."
"Also, he must not climb on the sofa."
"He slept only in his bed."
"If I say 'Tommy, come here', he will come quickly."
I give Tommy's leash back to Anitha.
"Was it difficult for Maya to look after him?" she asks.
"Oh no, I did not have any difficulty," I say.
Anitha happily thanks me.
She and Tommy go back.
